        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/api.ts:34",
            "finding": "\"`order.total`\" is now in cents (\"`cartTotal`\" returns \"`Cents`\"), but \"`toResponse`\" still formats it with \"`formatEuro`\", which treats its input as euros, so API totals are 100x too high (e.g. \"`2500.00 EUR`\" for 25 EUR); \"`formatAmount(order.total, order.currency)`\" is the matching helper."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:29,51-52",
            "finding": "\"`options.tags.push(\"bulk\")`\" mutates the shared module-level \"`DEFAULT_OPTIONS.tags`\" array, so after one bulk order every later order created with default options gets a \"`bulk`\" tag, and all of those orders share one array (\"`tags: options.tags`\")."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:82-88",
            "finding": "\"`saveOrder`\" is async but is no longer awaited, so its rejection (e.g. \"`order ... already exists`\") skips the \"`catch`\": reservations are not released, the rejection is unhandled, and the confirmation is sent for an order that was never stored."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:63-65",
            "finding": "The duplicate-SKU check runs after all items are reserved and throws without \"`releaseAll(reservedItems)`\", so every rejected duplicate-SKU order leaves its stock reserved permanently; the check should run before reserving."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:21",
            "finding": "\"`refundOrder`\" does not pass \"`order.currency`\" to \"`issueRefund`\", so the \"`\"EUR\"`\" default applies and refunds for \"`CHF`\" orders are recorded and shown as EUR; this undermines the new currency-aware \"`handleRefund`\" output."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DESIGN",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/order.ts:21,33-35",
            "finding": "\"`Order.customer`\" was made optional even though \"`createOrder`\" always requires a \"`Customer`\", so it needs a dead runtime check in \"`validateOrder`\" and a non-null assertion \"`order.customer!.email`\" in \"`src/notify.ts:7`\"; the change weakens type safety for no gain."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/cart.ts:18-40",
            "finding": "\"`topItem`\", \"`isValidCart`\" and \"`describeCode`\" (\"`src/discount.ts:38`\") have no callers anywhere in the code base; they are unused speculative additions riding along with the order-handling change."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "TESTING",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "package.json:6-8",
            "finding": "The repository has no tests and no test script, yet the commit changes the money unit, discount math and reservation and rollback paths; even one smoke test of \"`handleOrder`\" would have caught the \"`countUnits`\" crash and the percent-discount bug."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/order.ts:45-50",
            "finding": "The commit message \"Update order handling\" leaves out essential changes: the switch from euros to cents, the breaking change of the \"`createOrder`\" and \"`applyDiscount`\" signatures, the new minimum order value, and the new \"`units`\" field in the API response."
        }
    ]
}
